auth         = "advplyr"
version      = "@@VERSION@@"
descript     = "Audiobookshelf is a self-hosted audiobook and podcast server. Import your audiobook and podcast libraries, then stream to any device with the web player or the free iOS/Android companion apps - progress syncing, bookmarks, chapters, sleep timers and offline playback included. The server scans your library folders, fetches cover art and metadata, and handles podcast RSS downloads on your schedule. This package bundles the upstream single-executable build (embedded Node.js runtime and web client; media processing uses the system ffmpeg), runs as a dedicated unprivileged user in a hardened systemd sandbox, and listens on loopback only: the UI opens in a new browser tab via the standard TOS web route /audiobookshelf/, with no extra external port. Data is stored under /var/lib/audiobookshelf."
release_note = "Bundles the Audiobookshelf 2.36.0 upstream single-executable build (sha256-verified); transcoding uses the TOS system ffmpeg package. First launch initializes the database, then you create the admin account and add library folders. Grant the app user read/write access to your media share in TOS Control Panel - Shared Folders before adding it as a library path."
important    = "First visitor creates the admin account - complete the setup right after installing. Library folders on TOS shares must be granted to the app user 'audiobookshelf' via shared-folder permissions. The web UI has no default password on a fresh install. Data in /var/lib/audiobookshelf is kept by 'apt remove' and deleted by 'apt purge'."

